    statement;
}

The "initialization" is what gets executed the first time through the loop, the "condition" is what gets checked before each iteration, and the "increment" is what gets executed after each iteration.  In the for loop, the "statement" gets executed once for each iteration.  In the while loop, the statement gets executed at least once.  If the condition is always true, then the loop will never end.  If the condition is false, then the loop will stop executing the statement and move on to the next iteration of the program.

